==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|en|Mogor||obsolete}}
* {{alter|en|Mogul}}
* {{alter|en|Mughal}}

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|fa|مغول|tr=moğul}} and {{bor|en|ur|مغل}}, an Arabic and Persian corruption of {{m|en|Mongol}}, ultimately from {{der|en|xng|ᠮᠣᠩᠭᠤᠯ}}.<ref>Dodgson, Marshall G.S. (2009). The Venture of Islam. Volume 3: The Gunpowder Empires and Modern Times. University of Chicago Press. p. 62.</ref> More at [[w:Mughal Empire#Name|Mughal]].

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A head of the Timurid [[dynasty]] founded by Zahīr-ud-Dīn Muhammed Bābur (1483-1530) which controlled large parts of southern Asia from the 16th to the 19th centuries.
# {{lb|en|now|_|historical}} A [[Mongol]] or [[Mongolian]], especially a member or follower of the Moghul dynasty.
# An [[important]] or [[successful]] person; a [[magnate]]. (Now usually as {{m|en|mogul}}.)

